      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: actually yeah i do i have multiple people in discord we chat to who did tests. they performed on the old funland and discovered it stayed in memory even after switching maps multiple times.. 1001 did a proper test.. but its not just linked to that old world of mine this happened in lakuza's and he has a crash dump but its the same old unity error as always.. everyone crashed at the time.. but they all went down .. going by their hardware.. aka the less memory someone had boop they went down straight off the bat.\n\nThis video made of the dev meetup today.. where it happened to everyone in there. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dVN3m8kEk4E&feature=youtu.be&t=6414\n\nThe result as i discussed it with lakuza is more than likely a suspect IK.. but to crash everyone and overload memory like that is preety serious.. i've also noted many people crashing of late and i suspect that its 2017 related.. but as for pooling that's all done on server so if and when we upgrade to 2017 i do wonder if we will see an improvement because its preety bad currently.. and you know that people have mentioned memory leaks for ages.. its definitely linked with pooling.. if you want more detailed information i will have to run tests on the client.. but i cant exactly tell whats going on server side as that's kinda your job..",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
