  "details": "I have always seen user's going on about how much my old funland stayed in their memory and so i looked into it.. i don't want those issues again.. \n\nToday i heard from Lakuza who was at a dev meetup with Cyan and many more.. they all crashed at random times but all based on their individual hardware Lakuza even had someone say he had to restart because his memory was overloaded..\n\nThis is object pooling.. i don't have a clue what your using on the server but you need to change what happens when a user switches maps.. as that previous map should clean up and drop from memory. It should not stay their persisting causing more to build up from the next map alone and eventually causing instability due to an overload which most refer to as a \"Memory Leak\" \n\nSeeing as we are using the 2017 now.. i hope that when we are live with it, things will be a tad different because the pooling as of right now.. and has been for a long time is absolutely awful.\n\nMy only request is that when a user walks through a portal or visits a new world from the UI.. on connection to new world the old is dropped from memory.. nothing more to be said on the subject really.. its not limited to a 2017 client as people have been reporting issues with crashes & more for a long time.",
